The callback is not needed. `let x; const v = [(x = 5), -(x = 10)]; return <Stub v={v} x={x++} />` in the component body gives `x: 5`.

Three things have to be there:

- An earlier `x = K1` whose value goes to something that does not fold (an array element, a call argument).
- A later `x = K2` in the same statement whose value goes to something that constant propagation folds: `-(x = 10)`, `!(x = 10)`, `(x = 10) % 3`, `` `${x = 10}` ``, `o[(x = 10)]`.
