        jsx_runtime.jsx("_Underscore", {})   // string literal
      ]
    }), $[0] = t0;
  else t0 = $[0];
  return t0;
};
At runtime React renders it as an unknown custom element (<_underscore>), so the component never mounts and its subtree is empty. No build warning and no runtime error.

Same for $-prefixed names (<$Dollar /> → "$Dollar"). Member expressions are unaffected (<Nested._Inner /> stays a member expression), and ordinary capitalized names are fine.

Why this matters in practice
Lingui's babel macro rewrites <Trans> (from @lingui/react/macro) into the runtime component under a _Trans binding. With reactCompiler: true every translated element is emitted as jsx("_Trans", { id, message }), so a production build renders:

